pw-airplay changes to OwnTone 29.3 (owntone/owntone-server tag 29.3)

OwnTone is used as the AirPlay 2 sending engine, fed with live audio through
a named pipe. These changes adapt it to that use:

- Live pipe start (input.c, player.c, pipe_start_buffer_ms): playback of a
  pipe starts once this much audio is buffered instead of ~2 s, and buffered
  audio beyond it is dropped when the player clock starts, so the time spent
  connecting to the speakers does not end up as permanent extra latency.
  End to end latency is then the same in every session.
- Remote commands (input.c, httpd_dacp.c, airplay_events.c,
  pipe_remote_fifo): while a pipe plays, play/pause/next/previous from the
  speakers are written to a fifo for the application feeding the pipe,
  instead of acting on OwnTone's own queue. The AirPlay event parser also
  understands "plps" and the numeric modernMediaRemoteCommand form.
- MediaRemote (outputs/airplay.c): Apple receivers announcing bplist now
  playing support get registered as a MediaRemote now playing source with
  POST /command requests, the shape a real iPhone sends (as documented by the
  cliairplay project). This makes HomePods report title and play state.
- Network exposure (main.c, misc.c, httpd*.c, mdns_publish,
  http_bind_address): no advertising as an iTunes/DAAP library, only the DACP
  service the speakers need. DACP requests from a speaker we stream to are
  authorized by its Active-Remote id rather than by network trust.
- Build (configure.ac): the librespot-c subproject is not configured, so
  building without Spotify support does not require protobuf-c.

Apply with: git apply owntone-29.3.patch

